WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.016
Booking a class should not mean navigating a maze of forms.

00:00:04.351 --> 00:00:10.032
EasyLayer helps people choose, review, and finish one task, with a clear next
step.

00:00:10.588 --> 00:00:13.407
This is an Alexa Plus experience simulation.

00:00:13.681 --> 00:00:17.590
The hosted demo uses sample data, and never creates a real appointment.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:19.644
Let's try a pottery workshop.

00:00:20.148 --> 00:00:24.670
EasyLayer keeps the provider, date, duration, and price visible.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:30.048
Choose an available time, or use the guided command, later, to move to the
next option.

00:00:30.386 --> 00:00:33.471
A selected time becomes a draft, not a booking.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:37.427
The summary makes it clear what will happen before anything is submitted.

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:39.649
Now imagine getting interrupted.

00:00:39.957 --> 00:00:41.830
Pause the task, then resume it.

00:00:42.155 --> 00:00:45.083
The same draft returns with the same details.

00:00:45.368 --> 00:00:48.146
Progress is kept in this browser for the demonstration.

00:00:48.517 --> 00:00:51.806
Next, review the appointment and explicitly approve it.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:56.249
The demo uses a fictional contact, so no personal information is needed.

00:00:56.588 --> 00:00:59.021
Approved still does not mean booked.

00:00:59.382 --> 00:01:03.650
Here is the difficult case: a response is lost after submission.

00:01:03.985 --> 00:01:08.249
The simulator creates one sample record, but the result stays uncertain.

00:01:08.505 --> 00:01:10.883
It does not tell the user the booking succeeded.

00:01:11.242 --> 00:01:13.976
Repeated attempts do not create another record.

00:01:14.348 --> 00:01:17.841
EasyLayer asks the person to check the existing result instead.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:22.535
When the sample record is read back and matches, the status becomes verified.

00:01:22.855 --> 00:01:24.701
The record counter stays at one.

00:01:25.125 --> 00:01:29.933
Try the second scenario: the selected time becomes unavailable before
submission.

00:01:30.201 --> 00:01:35.059
EasyLayer stops, explains what changed, and requires a new choice and review.

00:01:35.546 --> 00:01:39.800
The downloadable Python project contains the self-hosted MCP server,
persistent drafts,

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:43.584
and an adapter targeting Easy Appointments.

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:46.230
The current hosted demo is browser-only.

00:01:46.412 --> 00:01:50.115
It is not connected to native Alexa or a live booking service.

00:01:50.377 --> 00:01:56.704
The earlier backend release recorded one hundred and seventeen passing
automated tests using controlled sources.

00:01:56.963 --> 00:02:00.560
Real service and real user validation remain next steps.

00:02:00.952 --> 00:02:07.752
EasyLayer is built around a simple promise: clear choices, recoverable
progress, and an honest result.

00:02:08.017 --> 00:02:12.649
Try the interactive demo, explore the failure scenarios, and inspect the
source.

